cff-version: 1.2.0
title: >-
  agent-evidence-vocabulary: a closed term registry for adversarial-execution
  evidence claims
message: >-
  If a term or crosswalk-match verdict from this registry is cited, cite a
  released version. A registry is a moving target until it is tagged, so a
  citation of the branch names whatever it happens to hold when someone follows it.
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Gilda
    given-names: Sankalp
    email: sankalp.gilda@gmail.com
    orcid: 'https://orcid.org/0000-0002-3645-4501'
repository-code: https://github.com/probityai/agent-evidence
abstract: >-
  A closed, versioned vocabulary for terms that describe adversarial-execution
  evidence claims: observation vantage, observation directness, containment
  posture, coverage denominators, and related evidence-quality dimensions.
  Independent implementations file crosswalks declaring how their own emitted
  claims map onto these terms. Companion project to agent-evidence-vectors
  (https://github.com/probityai/agent-evidence-vectors), which hosts the predicate
  spec this vocabulary describes and its conformance vector suite.
# Two licenses, deliberately. vocabulary.yaml (the registry data itself) is
# CC0-1.0, so a term can be reused, forked, or quoted with no attribution owed
# to anyone. The surrounding repository (documents, validator, CI) is
# Apache-2.0. See LICENSE and vocabulary.yaml's header.
license: [Apache-2.0, CC0-1.0]
version: 0.8.0
date-released: "2026-10-26"
